I have just been informed of another error in our nethack,
here at Oakland University.  We are currently running an
un-changed 3.0, with patches 1-4 applied.  We have the
pretty standard problem with shops buying un-purchased
items back.  This next error was sent to me by a user.

Preliminary data:

The user read a scroll of punishment and decided to pick up his
iron ball and wielded it.  All was find, bashing monsters with
the ball till he decided to go down stairs.  It gave him an
error (unknown message content) saying to talk to me about
me getting his character working again.  I went into the 
/save directory and his character had a .e included in the
title.  Renamed it without the .e, and he went on.  Next
scroll he read was a teleport scroll.  Got the same error
as above, but on the save a segmentation fault error.
I assume his character is gone.  Haven't checked the save
directory to see if there is a save file, but I doubt there
is.  Thought the nethack wizards should know.

